# Unit Approve grounding (every project)

Use this playbook for **any** SUT repo. Never hardcode one product’s domain (Evidence, Order, …) into AITest protocol or shared examples.

## Progressive match (SoT — AITest then sync MD)

```
Module → Function → Title → index.db (path/symbol) → prefer *Handler/*Service → write path:/code: → sync MD to SUT
```

| Step | Input | Effect on index.db |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | **Module** (Requirement Studio title) | Scope / lock **source-module family** folders (fail-closed if Latin/alias tokens miss all paths; else feature-folder discover) |
| 2 | **Function** of the TC (`tc.module`) | Rank / discover **files inside that family** (bridges + preferTokens) |
| 3 | **Title** (+ steps/expected) | Refine symbols/paths **only inside that family**; prefer `*CommandHandler` / `*Service` |
| 4 | Body-rule (optional) | Confirm excerpt patterns when intent needs it; same-family ties are **not** ambiguity |

Machine keys in sync MD: `requirement:` = Module; `function:` / legacy `module:` = Function.

Soft writeBack must **not** latch Auth/Mail/Notification/signed-URL generators unless Module tokens hit that stem. Wrong **domain** folders are blocked by moduleGate fail-closed + feature-folder discover — not by product denylists.

## Portable vs optional override

| Portable (AITest) | Per-project (SUT) — optional |
| --- | --- |
| Progressive Module→Function→Title on `index.db` | `.ai-test/code-aliases.json` nudge only |
| IT verbs in `GENERIC_VI_*` + `UNIT_INTENT_DEFS` | Manual `path:` / `code:` on one TC |
| Logic-layer + same-family Handler prefer | `sutMap` / `domainGuards` pins |

**Empty SUT knobs are valid.** `sutMap={}`, `domainGuards=[]`, missing `code-aliases.json` / `unit-intent-rules.json` must still Approve from `index.db`.

## Forbidden

- Product nouns in `viCodeAliases.ts` / protocol
- Treating same-family Create/Handler/Delete score ties as skip (`ambiguous margin`)
- Absolute `D:/...` paths in markers
- Copying another project’s `code-aliases.json`
- **Agent inventing/filling** SUT `.ai-test/code-aliases.json`, `sutMap`, `domainGuards`, or `unit-intent-rules.json` with product nouns — fix ranking in AITest instead

## After changes

Restart AITest Desktop → Approve again → MD must show `path:` / `code:` (not only `# sut-resolve: skipped`).
